WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.858
- Please welcome Soman Chainani.

00:00:01.858 --> 00:00:04.433
(crowd cheering)

00:00:04.433 --> 00:00:08.507
- So, meet everybody, I
don't know if y'all met.

00:00:08.507 --> 00:00:10.500
Um, I always love having
like a mixture of people

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:12.190
that might never be together in one place.

00:00:12.190 --> 00:00:13.110
That's my favorite part.

00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:14.510
- He was my Friday night date.

00:00:14.510 --> 00:00:15.869
When I was in high school.

00:00:15.869 --> 00:00:17.055
I have no social life.

00:00:17.055 --> 00:00:17.888
- Did he put out?

00:00:17.888 --> 00:00:19.626
(laughing)

00:00:19.626 --> 00:00:22.070
- X Files was my thing
every, every Friday.

00:00:22.070 --> 00:00:22.903
- I Remember.

00:00:22.903 --> 00:00:25.720
- Can I just say, you gorgeous.

00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:26.553
- Oh god.

00:00:26.553 --> 00:00:28.419
- Oh, you so good lookin'.

00:00:28.419 --> 00:00:29.252
Geez.

00:00:29.252 --> 00:00:30.085
- Thank you

00:00:30.085 --> 00:00:31.820
- I just wanted to
compliment you. I'm sorry.

00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:34.738
I'm somebody's black
mama, but you gorgeous.

00:00:34.738 --> 00:00:35.571
(laughing)

00:00:35.571 --> 00:00:36.910
(clapping)

00:00:36.910 --> 00:00:39.450
- My mom is going to appreciate that.

00:00:39.450 --> 00:00:41.660
My, my mom's upset I'm still single.

00:00:41.660 --> 00:00:43.483
So she's gonna, that's
going to be a calling card

00:00:43.483 --> 00:00:46.339
she's gonna send out to every
Indian in the tri-state area.

00:00:46.339 --> 00:00:48.640
- Just a reminder, you could
be in a horrible relationship.

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:50.090
So single ain't that bad.

00:00:50.090 --> 00:00:51.530
- I'm happy.

00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:54.030
- Um, I didn't even know this was a thing,

00:00:54.030 --> 00:00:56.700
but you studied fairytales at Harvard.

00:00:56.700 --> 00:00:58.664
So I could have gone to Harvard.

00:00:58.664 --> 00:00:59.497
(laughing)

00:00:59.497 --> 00:01:00.790
I feel like wait, what?

00:01:00.790 --> 00:01:02.557
Like, fairytales?

00:01:02.557 --> 00:01:03.580
- Yeah, they didn't know
it was a thing either,

00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:06.100
but I grew up at Disney baby.

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:08.170
Like I was the kid whose parents,

00:01:08.170 --> 00:01:09.270
when they couldn't deal with them,

00:01:09.270 --> 00:01:11.431
like plop them in front
of Alice in Wonderland or

00:01:11.431 --> 00:01:12.264
Cinderella.

00:01:12.264 --> 00:01:13.097
- Absolutely, Lion King all the way down.

00:01:13.097 --> 00:01:13.930
The way that, you know,

00:01:13.930 --> 00:01:15.354
parents use Tik ToK and YouTube today.

00:01:15.354 --> 00:01:17.100
Like Disney was our thing.

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:20.270
I never stick an iPad
in front of my children.

00:01:20.270 --> 00:01:21.103
Others do.

00:01:21.103 --> 00:01:23.840
- But, you know, so I knew
all those stories by heart,

00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:26.570
but then I went to college and
ended up sort of by chance in

00:01:26.570 --> 00:01:27.403
this fairytales class.

00:01:27.403 --> 00:01:28.236
- Yeah.

00:01:28.236 --> 00:01:30.560
- And I thought we were gonna
learn the Disney versions.

00:01:30.560 --> 00:01:32.860
Cause I thought Disney invented
all these stories, you know?

00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:33.994
(laughing)

00:01:33.994 --> 00:01:35.480
Cause I didn't know any better.

00:01:35.480 --> 00:01:37.100
And then, you learn the original
stories and you're like,

00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:40.980
these stories are so rich and
dangerous and provocative and

00:01:40.980 --> 00:01:42.960
the evil guy wins half the
time and the good guy and

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:44.880
there's, there's an edge to it.

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:46.930
I felt like, like my mind was blown.

00:01:46.930 --> 00:01:49.330
I'm like my whole childhood is
based on this lie. You know?

00:01:49.330 --> 00:01:51.080
Like how do I,

00:01:51.080 --> 00:01:53.810
how can I bring these
stories to other people?

00:01:53.810 --> 00:01:56.290
And I think that's where this
new book came from this idea

00:01:56.290 --> 00:01:57.810
of like, why can't kids grow up with

00:01:57.810 --> 00:02:00.010
that kind of danger in their fairytale.

00:02:00.010 --> 00:02:01.400
So it feels more like,

00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:02.870
you don't know who's
going to win at the end.

00:02:02.870 --> 00:02:04.780
And I think that's what
I wanted to do with it

00:02:04.780 --> 00:02:06.610
is give evil an equal chance.

00:02:06.610 --> 00:02:07.960
So that's why even in
"School for Good and Evil"

00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:08.940
and in "Beast and Beauty",

00:02:08.940 --> 00:02:11.420
there's always a balance beast
and beauty, good and evil.

00:02:11.420 --> 00:02:13.080
- I love that this is your slogan.

00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:15.090
Give evil an equal chance.

00:02:15.090 --> 00:02:16.570
(laughing)

00:02:16.570 --> 00:02:19.860
- Listen, I wish I could
go back to high school

00:02:20.820 --> 00:02:23.550
and run for every election on that.

00:02:23.550 --> 00:02:25.710
- Oh well Soman's first book,
"The school for Good and Evil"

00:02:25.710 --> 00:02:27.750
is now an upcoming movie
with Charlize Theron

00:02:27.750 --> 00:02:30.168
and Kerry Washington. That's crazy goal.

00:02:30.168 --> 00:02:31.960
(crowd clapping)

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:35.358
So, what was it like, like seeing your,

00:02:35.358 --> 00:02:37.360
your dream and your vision and you know,

00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:38.953
all your words come to life on screen?

00:02:38.953 --> 00:02:40.620
- I mean, I almost had a heart attack,

00:02:40.620 --> 00:02:42.080
I think like when you first,

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:44.410
cause I was in quarantine
before I went onto set.

00:02:44.410 --> 00:02:46.820
So you're alone in a room
for multiple days being like,

00:02:46.820 --> 00:02:49.450
okay, visualizing it, being
like be cool, be cool.

00:02:49.450 --> 00:02:51.628
And as soon as you get on
set, not cool, you know.

00:02:51.628 --> 00:02:53.584
- It's Kerry Washington
and Charlize Theron, yeah.

00:02:53.584 --> 00:02:54.900
- And also, it's Paul Feig, the director,

00:02:54.900 --> 00:02:56.797
and he's just visionary,
you know, "Bridesmaids",

00:02:56.797 --> 00:02:58.330
"Freaks and Geeks" by.

00:02:58.330 --> 00:03:01.160
And he doesn't like green
screen and pixels and just

00:03:01.160 --> 00:03:02.750
everything being computer generated.

00:03:02.750 --> 00:03:05.570
So he built the entire freaking
school for good and evil.

00:03:05.570 --> 00:03:08.195
Like, you go onto set
and it is this massive

00:03:08.195 --> 00:03:10.310
like complex of the school.

00:03:10.310 --> 00:03:11.240
And so to go in there,

00:03:11.240 --> 00:03:13.600
and I had spent 10 years
writing these books.

00:03:13.600 --> 00:03:16.440
10 years of like all my
unconscious and everything

00:03:16.440 --> 00:03:18.130
suddenly projected out.

00:03:18.130 --> 00:03:20.460
I kept having these like little
psychic breaks where I kept

00:03:20.460 --> 00:03:23.173
forgetting it was my kinda universe.

00:03:23.173 --> 00:03:26.090
- You're like, who created
this? They're amazing!

00:03:26.090 --> 00:03:27.120
- It happened once where

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:28.550
I went to the costume department

00:03:28.550 --> 00:03:30.070
and I was like, oh, that's so weird,

00:03:30.070 --> 00:03:32.580
there's a character named
Hort in my books, how strange.

00:03:32.580 --> 00:03:34.100
Like, just like totally

00:03:34.100 --> 00:03:34.933
- Out of body

00:03:34.933 --> 00:03:36.300
- Out of body complete, you know.

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:39.100
But, um, I just think it's gonna be,

00:03:39.100 --> 00:03:40.020
it's a huge movie.

00:03:40.020 --> 00:03:41.620
It's one of Netflix's biggest movies ever.

00:03:41.620 --> 00:03:42.980
And I just think it's,

00:03:42.980 --> 00:03:45.500
it gives them that kind of
Harry Potter esque franchise,

00:03:45.500 --> 00:03:47.370
but this time a little more representative

00:03:47.370 --> 00:03:48.970
a little bit more inclusive.

00:03:48.970 --> 00:03:50.030
You know, and I think it's just,

00:03:50.030 --> 00:03:51.680
it's a great movie for our times.

